        "id": 1039624
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T22:44:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are meant to be handled by a BluestoreDevice class that wraps the Backend and manages concurrency. This commit covers the engine and enough of the Python layer to pass test_basic.py.",
      "parentUuid": "1e2bbb89_23cc7d55",
      "revId": "633054551671766058f39473e6d1a1a88bf1906c",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "441f9197_47890e5b",
        "filename": "bluestore/src/bluestore/diskfile.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039387
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T14:25:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "self.object \u003d tombstone drops the last reference to the retired object. ~Object() then does a blocking commit under the GIL. Same for the local prev in Writer.put(). Both hit the normal overwrite and delete path.",
      "revId": "633054551671766058f39473e6d1a1a88bf1906c",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01302901_aa5069fd",
        "filename": "bluestore/src/bluestore/diskfile.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039624
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T22:44:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "True. in fact, all of our writes are currently done under the GIL. This is because our object model requires our state changes to happen under lock (in our case the GIL), but queuing our transactions can also block the thread. Since submitting our transactions outside the lock risks reordering them, for now we fully write under the GIL. In the next commit, which focuses on concurrency, I will change the engine api to prevent this.",
      "parentUuid": "441f9197_47890e5b",
      "revId": "633054551671766058f39473e6d1a1a88bf1906c",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3fcb0a0e_5f22b6d9",
        "filename": "bluestore/src/bluestore/diskfile.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 125,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039387
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T14:25:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The old reader quarantined when bytes read didn\u0027t match Content-Length, or the streamed MD5 didn\u0027t match the ETag. This one streams whatever read() returns, so a truncated or corrupt object is served silently.",
      "revId": "633054551671766058f39473e6d1a1a88bf1906c",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cfd83be8_d3b12fa7",
        "filename": "bluestore/src/bluestore/diskfile.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 125,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039624
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-23T22:44:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the check can only complete once the object has been fully read, it would be too late to change the response. Such a system would only give us a log line. Thankfully, BlueStore checksums its own data and fails the read on a mismatch, so this isn\u0027t a great concern.",
      "parentUuid": "3fcb0a0e_5f22b6d9",
      "revId": "633054551671766058f39473e6d1a1a88bf1906c",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
